WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.225
Savings arrive as offices move at their
MPLS renewal dates, not on day one.

2
00:00:05.225 --> 00:00:09.126
In the base case the program turns
cumulatively positive in year

3
00:00:09.126 --> 00:00:13.100
four and is about seven point seven
million ahead after five years.

4
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.682
The refresh spends fifty million up front,

5
00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:19.887
so the five-year difference is about
fifty-seven point seven million.

6
00:00:19.887 --> 00:00:23.212
But all of that turns on what
MPLS costs per office today.

7
00:00:23.212 --> 00:00:26.612
Breakeven is eight hundred
seventy-three dollars a month.

8
00:00:26.612 --> 00:00:29.188
Above it, the program pays for itself.

9
00:00:29.188 --> 00:00:33.563
Below it, it's still the better
architecture, argued on capability.

10
00:00:33.563 --> 00:00:34.900
Then there's security.
